I go to a spice stall.
There is an elderly man there.
I respectfully call him 'chacha'.
"Chacha, hello," I say.
"Hello, daughter," he says.
There are many colourful spices in the shop.
Their smell is very good.
Chacha shows me a special tea masala.
He gives me a little spice.
"Smell this, daughter," he says.
I smell the masala.
I like its aroma very much.
"This is very good," I say.
"I want a small packet."
"How much is this?" I ask.
"This is for only fifty rupees," Chacha says.
"Okay, please give me one packet," I say.
I give him fifty rupees.
He smiles and gives me the packet.
